notes: "The materials library is the part I use most. Assets are stored once, at their original size, with their source and usage. This figure is a real one: C1′–C1′ distances at twelve paired positions in PDB 1BNA, one public structure. They are not independent replicates, and not hydrogen-bond distances; I use them as an example of real evidence, not as a result of the editor. The figure is referenced, not re-pasted, so the labels and pixels survive."
